\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. How do Thy mercies close me round!
\par For ever be Thy name adored!
\par I blush in all things to abound;
\par The servant is above his Lord!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Inured to poverty and pain,
\par A suffering life my Master led;
\par The Son of God, the Son of Man,
\par He had not where to lay His head.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. But, lo, a place He hath prepared
\par For me, whom watchful angels keep;
\par Yea, He Himself becomes my guard,
\par He smooths my bed, and gives me sleep.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Jesus protects; my fears, begone!
\par What can the Rock of ages move?
\par Safe in my arms I lay me down,
\par Thy everlasting arms of love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. While Thou art intimately nigh,
\par Who, who shall violate my rest?
\par Sin, earth, and hell I now defy;
\par I lean upon my Saviour's breast.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. I rest beneath the Almighty's shade,
\par My griefs expire, my troubles cease:
\par Thou, Lord, on whom my soul is stayed,
\par Wilt keep me in perfect peace.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Me for Thine own Thou lov'st to take,
\par In time and in eternity;
\par Thou never, never wilt forsake
\par A helpless soul that trust in Thee.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

